e  and not decreasing the reasons for that  are actually quite deep and it took a  long time until physicists actually  understood the reasons for disorder  always to grow that's called the second  law of thermodynamics for a long time  the second law was actually an axiom was  another postulate that you added to the  classical mechanics we all know Newton  but much later it was understood that  this is actually a natural course of  events when you have many many particles  in the system when you have lots and  lots of particle degrees of freedom the  chaotic motion of particles which  interact with each other leads to the  increase of entropy and to the second  law of thermodynamics now  the comic book that we wrote was about  the imaginary creature that Maxwell  the famous physicist that invented  electromagnetism thought about as a way  of disputing the second law he said  there could be a creature essentially  like our ourselves that would put order  in things and you won't have to spend  any energy doing that you will just have  to open and shut the door and order  things separate hi separate the gases  between two different compartments into  a high pressure and low pressure or a  hot and a cold or reverse essentially  the arrow of time by just observing the  different particles and allowing and  disallowing them to move in certain ways  and that was a puzzle that was a paradox  that kept businesses busy for more than  60 years or 70 years until it was  understood that such a creature cannot  exist and therefore the second law of  thermodynamics was said this is actually  the topic that is explained in in our  book it's it's the fact that a Maxwell  demon is a demon is is not something  that we can design let's say nowadays  with robots and nano electronics it's a  impossibility in physics  and it's a quite tricky subject to to  understand and why is it important to  the sort of day-to-day lives of humans  in other words conceptually we may or  may not underst